WEBVTT

00:09.500 --> 00:12.110
Hehe... isn't this awesome?

00:13.620 --> 00:17.520
Are these... all yours?

00:18.120 --> 00:20.600
Ah, those are Mother's.

00:21.660 --> 00:26.580
Look, this part of the field is mine.

00:27.370 --> 00:29.880
I planted all of these.

00:32.110 --> 00:35.540
I put a lot of effort into raising this corn.

00:36.540 --> 00:38.650
They're very delicious.

00:41.480 --> 00:43.990
What should I plant next time?

00:45.680 --> 00:47.000
I don't know...

00:48.420 --> 00:49.090
What?

00:49.910 --> 00:53.760
Hey, as long as it's a vegetable, can you grow it here?

00:55.280 --> 00:56.720
Yeah, probably...

00:57.100 --> 00:59.220
Well, can you plant bananas here?

00:59.410 --> 01:03.300
Ehhh? That's not possible.

01:03.730 --> 01:05.410
Then, plant apples.

01:08.210 --> 01:10.730
That's not possible either...

01:11.140 --> 01:14.320
What? Didn't you say we could plant whatever we want here?

01:14.510 --> 01:17.860
Geez, your field isn't as good as you said.

01:19.500 --> 01:25.560
That's not true! Besides, bananas and apples aren't vegetables.

01:26.600 --> 01:28.560
R-Really?

01:28.980 --> 01:35.000
Yeah. You're showing off all the time...
But you don't even know this?

01:37.730 --> 01:40.580
W-What? You're the only farmer!

01:40.830 --> 01:44.390
I grew up in the city. It's okay for me to not know that.

01:46.650 --> 01:47.980
What's that supposed to mean?

01:50.370 --> 01:54.860
What's wrong with you and your weird fish?
You always pin it in your hair.

01:55.400 --> 01:56.660
It looks old-fashioned.

01:58.540 --> 02:03.020
Ah, what are you doing? This is my special fish.

02:03.260 --> 02:05.770
Special? How is it special?

02:06.030 --> 02:09.840
T-This... well... It's a secret.

02:10.110 --> 02:11.520
What was that?

02:11.840 --> 02:17.610
Anyway, this is a poor fishy.
It didn't do anything bad anyway.

02:19.920 --> 02:22.850
Geez, you owe me one this time.

02:23.700 --> 02:24.590
Owe you?

02:24.760 --> 02:26.360
Yeah, you owe me.

02:30.810 --> 02:35.820
Small Cousin and Fireworks

02:55.320 --> 02:57.110
Geez, why should I do this?

03:05.360 --> 03:07.160
Shoot, I have to hurry up!

03:50.910 --> 03:53.460
Huh? Hikari-chan is going to come here today?

03:54.140 --> 03:56.350
It's going to be fun again.

03:58.240 --> 04:00.320
I think it's going to be troublesome.

04:01.300 --> 04:02.400
What's wrong?

04:03.360 --> 04:04.140
Wait for a second.

04:05.040 --> 04:05.880
Ken-chan?

04:24.700 --> 04:27.240
Well, let's start from the first question and check our answers.

04:27.240 --> 04:34.490
Number one, the square root of 5. Number two, 1/125. Number three, 65356.

04:33.410 --> 04:35.840
Hey, did you hear something strange?

04:34.490 --> 04:36.190
So far, every question is worth two points.

04:36.200 --> 04:37.770
You worry too much.

04:36.200 --> 04:37.770
If you got all of them right, then you got all six points.

04:38.700 --> 04:40.220
Well, whoever didn't get this problem...

04:41.060 --> 04:44.650
Atano, you don't want to have a good summer vacation?

04:45.450 --> 04:46.810
Now, let's check the answers for the second part.

05:02.610 --> 05:08.700
3.1699... Every question is worth 3 points.

05:03.030 --> 05:08.700
I can hear that weird sound coming from you, Ken-chan.

05:08.700 --> 05:10.860
If you got all of them right, you get 12 points.

05:10.860 --> 05:12.230
This...

05:10.860 --> 05:12.230
Whoever didn't get it...

05:13.550 --> 05:18.110
Atano, be ready to spend the entire summer with me.

05:16.710 --> 05:18.110
Are you okay?

05:20.080 --> 05:20.950
Hey, Tomosaka-san.

05:25.470 --> 05:26.460
You're loud.

05:39.870 --> 05:42.140
Hey, I did hear something weird here.

05:42.710 --> 05:44.840
I told you, that's not right.

05:45.260 --> 05:47.610
<i>You</i> are not right!

05:48.110 --> 05:51.860
Anyway, why do you have your hand in your backpack?

05:51.910 --> 05:53.210
T-This is...

05:53.450 --> 05:54.750
That's strange...

06:01.120 --> 06:05.810
Come on, take your hand out of the backpack. Hurry, hurry, hurry!

06:06.200 --> 06:07.940
You're so persistent.

06:08.680 --> 06:11.010
For someone as persistent as you, I'll do this...

06:11.990 --> 06:13.720
Hermit crab!!

06:17.920 --> 06:19.740
The result isn't bad.

06:29.990 --> 06:33.970
Kenji. Hey, Hikari-chan will be here today, right?

06:35.300 --> 06:37.540
She's earlier than usual.

06:37.880 --> 06:39.800
How do you know?

06:40.230 --> 06:42.050
Suzuka-chan told me.

06:44.020 --> 06:46.970
That girl, it's her again...

06:47.280 --> 06:49.900
Hey, let's go to the bus station and pick her up, okay?

06:51.100 --> 06:52.420
Yeah.

06:53.230 --> 06:55.020
It's fine, forget her.

06:55.370 --> 06:56.780
She'll come anyway.

06:57.040 --> 06:59.510
What? Do you really mean that?

06:59.910 --> 07:01.710
Yeah, I mean it.

07:02.950 --> 07:05.120
Come on, you are so cold.

07:06.150 --> 07:10.880
Well, that's fine. I'll go by myself.

07:14.100 --> 07:16.040
I'm not cold, am I?

07:17.480 --> 07:22.280
Hey, I think we should go to the bus station and pick her up. She doesn't come here often.

07:22.430 --> 07:25.730
Yeah, we should pick her up sometime.

07:26.780 --> 07:32.030
Ah? You looked at your backpack just now.
Are you thinking up some weird thing to do to her?

07:33.830 --> 07:35.660
What? What weird plan?

07:36.280 --> 07:39.930
That's because you have that hermit crab with you.

07:44.230 --> 07:47.230
Geez, you're really persistent, aren't you?

07:50.900 --> 07:52.810
You're really persistent, aren't you?

07:53.360 --> 07:56.050
I don't have the hermit crab with me.

08:00.580 --> 08:01.550
Hey, Nanami.

08:08.630 --> 08:10.810
Tokyo special permission-given agency director.

08:08.630 --> 08:17.870
(Tl Note: "Tokyo special permission-given agency director," is a Japanese tongue twister.)

08:11.280 --> 08:17.370
Ah... well... Tokyo special... giv...gi...gi...

08:19.850 --> 08:24.020
I got you! It's not that easy to mimic me, Nanami-sensei.

08:25.190 --> 08:27.680
Sorry, sorry.

08:27.790 --> 08:29.870
You two are still that close to each other.

08:31.110 --> 08:32.110
Hi... ka... ri-chan.

08:31.110 --> 08:32.110
Hikari.

08:33.650 --> 08:35.070
Yo, guys!

08:41.300 --> 08:43.810
Well... next bus...

08:45.010 --> 08:47.740
What? 8 hours later?

08:50.720 --> 08:55.480
Geez, don't come to school all of a sudden without notifying us.

08:56.810 --> 09:01.330
This is nothing bad. I'm here to say hi to my old uncle.

09:01.840 --> 09:03.040
Anyway, Hikari...

09:06.910 --> 09:09.020
Ah? What is that?

09:11.710 --> 09:13.420
You thought I'd be scared by your little tricks?

09:16.910 --> 09:18.760
I am not a kid anymore.

09:20.240 --> 09:23.460
Hikari-chan is still very energetic.

09:23.600 --> 09:27.390
And she's even older than me by a year... So unbelievable.

09:29.050 --> 09:30.300
Hey, what are you going to do today?

09:30.410 --> 09:33.760
Hmm, I am going to fix my motorbike.

09:33.910 --> 09:36.310
Ah, you're fixing it again?

09:36.410 --> 09:40.410
Yeah, this year it seems like it needs more work.

09:41.380 --> 09:44.510
Hey, if you get it fixed, can you take me fishing?

09:44.910 --> 09:47.380
Well, let me think about it.

09:56.370 --> 09:58.060
So hot...

09:59.360 --> 10:00.870
It's really hot.

10:02.030 --> 10:05.990
Ah, I can't take it anymore. I'll rest a bit.

10:13.320 --> 10:15.320
Huh? She went to the field?

10:15.740 --> 10:20.450
Yeah. And she's so forgetful. She left her hat here again.

10:20.960 --> 10:22.910
Not again.

10:23.170 --> 10:25.890
Well, I'll take it to her.

10:26.310 --> 10:27.600
I'm sorry that I keep asking you for help.

10:28.310 --> 10:29.910
(Tl Note: Aloha is Hawaiian for "Hello" and "Goodbye.")

10:28.310 --> 10:29.910
Aloha!

10:35.370 --> 10:38.460
Hey you, did you go swimming already?

10:38.640 --> 10:42.440
Of course, I am here for swimming.

10:43.020 --> 10:45.630
Hey, how are you guys doing? You and Nanami?

10:45.960 --> 10:48.530
Is your relationship any closer?

10:50.040 --> 10:52.370
Hey, wait!

10:54.160 --> 10:55.740
I don't know what your purpose is.

10:56.200 --> 10:58.940
I'm really busy, don't you see that?

10:59.610 --> 11:00.660
Ah, I see.

11:01.390 --> 11:06.010
Well, let's play with fireworks tonight, and ask Nanami to come, okay?

11:06.400 --> 11:09.150
Okay? Okay?? Okay???

11:09.270 --> 11:12.940
Fireworks? Yeah, I'll think about it.

11:13.710 --> 11:14.410
Later!

11:30.310 --> 11:32.640
Geez, what a leisurely girl.

11:44.130 --> 11:45.580
Hey, Nanami.

11:46.400 --> 11:48.440
Huh? Ken-chan?

11:50.260 --> 11:56.860
Ah? Ken-chan, where are you hiding?

11:58.210 --> 12:00.400
Hint number one, Nanami special.

12:01.350 --> 12:02.740
Nanami special?

12:03.960 --> 12:06.530
Ah, the watermelon is wearing my hat.

12:05.730 --> 12:08.240
(Nanami special)

12:08.710 --> 12:12.150
Hehe, are you surprised?

12:14.910 --> 12:19.200
Hey, come on out.

12:21.800 --> 12:25.250
Hurry, hurry. If you can't find me, I will go back home.

12:27.810 --> 12:29.610
How could you...

12:30.700 --> 12:31.870
This is fun.

12:36.880 --> 12:37.660
Ah, it's a mole!

12:44.230 --> 12:47.350
Geez, I was scared by you again!

12:47.410 --> 12:50.260
I was the one who got scared.

12:51.600 --> 12:55.830
Anyway, you owe me one more favor.

12:56.630 --> 13:00.260
Add on this one, now it's 57 to 42.

13:00.430 --> 13:02.510
I know, I know.

13:04.400 --> 13:09.120
Anyway, when we first owed each other favors, it started here.

13:09.590 --> 13:11.190
Now you owe me a favor.

13:13.160 --> 13:16.300
But we can't reach 100 favors each year.

13:16.800 --> 13:17.690
That's true.

13:18.230 --> 13:23.720
Ah, I forgot to add the hermit crab in school. Now it's 58 to 42.

13:24.410 --> 13:26.560
Ah? I don't owe you from that.

13:27.130 --> 13:28.740
Of course you owe me.

13:29.600 --> 13:32.100
Geez, I can't deal with you under this situation.

13:34.990 --> 13:41.940
Yeah, I just met Hikari.
She asked me if I wanted to play with fireworks tonight.

13:42.420 --> 13:43.790
And she invited you as well.

13:44.310 --> 13:46.310
Ah, I want to go, I want to go!

13:50.710 --> 13:54.090
Geez... That guy is really slow.

13:54.390 --> 13:56.500
Who is 'that guy' you're talking about?

13:57.460 --> 13:58.710
Sorry for making you wait!

14:01.100 --> 14:02.000
Hatano?

14:02.470 --> 14:08.950
Well, actually I don't know what happened, but I saw a depressed teenager at the bus station.

14:09.560 --> 14:12.090
When I went there, it was Hatano-kun.

14:12.890 --> 14:14.330
So I asked him to buy some fireworks and bring them here.

14:14.510 --> 14:18.500
Yeah, as long as I can help Hikari-chan, I will do whatever I can do!

14:18.940 --> 14:23.130
What 'helping'? You're only being used as a slave.

14:23.850 --> 14:26.330
There are a lot.

14:26.880 --> 14:30.070
Yeah, you chose all the ones I wanted. Good job.

14:30.130 --> 14:33.770
Ah! Haha! Thank you so much!

14:34.550 --> 14:35.930
Let's start now.

14:36.270 --> 14:40.640
Okay. Let's start with the most beautiful ones.

14:41.380 --> 14:43.370
We have to have a good opening.

14:43.400 --> 14:45.840
I think we should save those until the end.

14:46.170 --> 14:49.820
What are you talking about? The start is very important.

14:50.480 --> 14:52.230
All right, let's go.

15:01.310 --> 15:02.520
Well, that's fine.

15:04.080 --> 15:05.300
Look, look.

15:23.370 --> 15:24.430
With pleasure...

15:26.230 --> 15:28.610
Wow, that's amazing, Hikari-chan.

15:29.040 --> 15:30.820
That's not amazing, that's dangerous.

15:31.370 --> 15:32.820
Huh? What?

15:33.720 --> 15:35.210
Don't point your fireworks at others.

15:40.090 --> 15:43.310
Wow, there is a little bear inside this one.

15:43.560 --> 15:46.340
Ah, that's only a little doll.

15:46.680 --> 15:49.190
And it has a parachute with it.

15:49.660 --> 15:51.100
That's so cute.

15:51.350 --> 15:53.840
The real one is cuter.

15:54.720 --> 15:58.500
Kenji said he will catch it for you. Let's play this!

15:58.510 --> 16:01.190
Ah? What did you say?

16:02.060 --> 16:04.120
I never promised that kind of troublesome stuff.

16:07.100 --> 16:08.080
Here goes!

16:10.420 --> 16:13.550
All right, for Nanami, go!

16:22.050 --> 16:23.730
All right, hurry up and go for it.

16:24.330 --> 16:26.900
Hey, why should I?

16:46.510 --> 16:49.010
Great, I caught it!

16:51.510 --> 16:54.290
Hikari-chan, a present for you.

16:55.200 --> 16:56.390
Hatano-kun.

17:01.010 --> 17:02.590
How come you're so dumb?

17:03.570 --> 17:07.060
It means nothing since you caught it, geez!

17:07.070 --> 17:08.110
Hikari-chan...

17:08.810 --> 17:13.830
Hey, let's do it again. How can I evade it now?

17:14.730 --> 17:18.360
That's good to hear. Actually, we have another one.

17:18.830 --> 17:19.710
Ken-chan.

17:23.590 --> 17:25.500
You really are not giving up.

17:25.900 --> 17:26.830
Shut up.

17:27.390 --> 17:28.940
Let's compete then.

17:29.380 --> 17:30.740
Don't slack off.

17:31.200 --> 17:34.680
Yeah, I'll show Hikari-chan how good I really am.

17:49.950 --> 17:51.760
All right!

18:02.440 --> 18:02.960
Here you go.

18:03.590 --> 18:04.720
Sorry, Hikari-chan.

18:05.160 --> 18:06.210
Ken-chan...

18:06.600 --> 18:11.270
Don't be mistaken, I was just trying to beat Hatano.

18:11.670 --> 18:14.200
I didn't catch it for you.

18:14.590 --> 18:17.740
I know, but, thank you.

18:18.140 --> 18:19.530
I will take care of it.

18:20.420 --> 18:23.670
You... still really like these weird things.

18:26.000 --> 18:30.350
What are you doing? Poor little bear...

18:31.750 --> 18:32.800
Yeah, yeah...

18:33.150 --> 18:36.590
And by saying, 'This poor bear is weird,' Little Bear will be sad.

18:36.750 --> 18:38.000
I know.

18:38.160 --> 18:39.150
He's not giving up.

18:41.460 --> 18:43.690
Ah, we don't have any more beautiful ones.

18:44.040 --> 18:48.760
You really should leave one for the end, Hikari-sensei.

18:52.690 --> 18:55.820
Hey, oniichan, let's play with sparklers together.

18:56.570 --> 18:58.760
Hey, that's not right, Suzuka-chan.

18:58.880 --> 19:00.150
Ah? Why?

19:00.790 --> 19:03.030
You should come this way.

19:04.900 --> 19:07.190
Hey, don't worry about weird stuff.

19:07.660 --> 19:09.520
And you over here too.

19:10.520 --> 19:11.380
Great!

19:13.380 --> 19:17.050
Um... What should we do?

19:17.620 --> 19:20.280
Hatano-kun, light this.

19:20.540 --> 19:21.130
Sure!

19:25.060 --> 19:27.010
My shoulders are tired...

19:27.860 --> 19:29.860
Leave it to me, Hikari-chan.

19:33.100 --> 19:34.370
I'm thirsty...

19:34.620 --> 19:37.010
I prepared for this earlier...

19:37.150 --> 19:38.830
You actually do have some sense...

19:41.900 --> 19:43.120
It doesn't have any ice...

19:43.670 --> 19:46.180
I don't want it after all, you can have it.

19:46.430 --> 19:49.090
Yay! Hikari-chan gave me a present!

19:52.550 --> 19:53.280
How pitiful...

19:56.110 --> 19:58.610
Look, the color changed.

19:59.260 --> 20:01.650
That looks cool, but it's only a sparkler.

20:03.410 --> 20:06.670
Hey, it's very beautiful.

20:10.700 --> 20:14.410
It'd be great if it never fades.

20:14.930 --> 20:17.280
Huh? Ah, yeah.

20:17.650 --> 20:23.440
Are you going to stay with me forever, Ken-chan?

20:24.240 --> 20:25.200
Nanami...

20:30.010 --> 20:30.940
W-Why did I bring this up?

21:04.210 --> 21:06.130
Hikari-chan, long time no see.

21:06.260 --> 21:07.690
Nanami, you haven't changed a bit.

21:07.810 --> 21:11.010
But, all the shovels and spades are new.

21:11.140 --> 21:12.030
Ah, I see...

21:12.130 --> 21:14.510
Hikari-chan, you haven't changed a bit.

21:14.640 --> 21:17.970
Are you saying that I am still little?

21:18.320 --> 21:19.270
No, not that...

21:19.390 --> 21:22.290
Let's have a talk then, Nanami-san.

21:24.770 --> 21:27.860
Next on Lamune: Student Council President and the Reward

21:26.860 --> 21:31.990
